[{"code":"program_shape","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":49,"col":77},"end":{"line":49,"col":83}},"title":"PROGRAM SHAPE","message":"Key `Restore` writes the whole model, a record of several fields, with a value\nthe compiler cannot see into, which hides which of its fields changed, so no\nbinding of the page can be chosen for it: `browser-inline` writes only the\nbindings a key's writes reach, and never checks the whole page again\n(`docs/design/browser-inline.md` §8.7; §5, class 3). Write the fields the arm\nchanges, as a record update of the model — `{ model | field = … }` — so that its\nwrites name them."}]
